your THINKING for this act, never your process — why you graded, closed, ruled or edited as you did, which is the substance the other side answers. The ledger already holds WHAT you did, in order, so an account of the verbs you ran narrates what the record reconstructs; --reason-file for anything long or from stdin with -

§3 (on 17 pages):
