$ feov-record edit --help
change the report — the only path into report.md, and how every repair lands

The ONLY path into blue/report.md — a raw write or a shell edit is denied.

TAKING RED'S FIX AS IT STANDS. Where red prescribed concrete replacement text on a gap, you can
apply THAT text rather than retyping it: the tool reads the span and the replacement off the gap
and edits with them, so you supply neither. Your argument for the change is still required and
still yours — accepting is a decision, not a transcription.

Why it exists: typing red's text yourself is the same act only if you get every byte right, and a
stray space or a re-wrapped line means you did what red asked while the record says you did not —
which costs you the estoppel that stops red re-opening its own words. Taking the text directly
makes the agreement structural.

You are never obliged to accept. Writing your own replacement is your right to disagree and is
recorded as one.

The tool matches your span across the invisible anchor layer and REFUSES a replacement that drops, duplicates or invents an anchor: a finding marker or a citation anchor may travel THROUGH your edit, never disappear in one.

An anchor INSIDE the text you are replacing must be copied verbatim into the replacement. One that merely sits at its edge is not inside it — a quote's trailing punctuation is trimmed before the span is located, so an anchor before a sentence's final period falls outside, is preserved for you, and typing it into the replacement is refused as inventing one. You are not asked to work out which: get it wrong either way and the refusal names the anchor and says which of the two it wants.

Quote enough context that the span matches exactly ONE place, or the edit is refused as ambiguous rather than applied to the wrong site.

WHAT MAY BE IN THE REPORT AT ALL: research prose written for a reader of the SUBJECT, and the markers this tool places. Nothing else — no provenance or attribution tags, no notes to another seat, no argument about the run, no narration of how the report was made. A fact that LIMITS THE CONCLUSION stays, re-voiced as a limit on the answer rather than a story about the attempt. Operational facts go to `log`, arguments to `position` or `closing`. The same rule is stated on every verb whose text the report prints: this one, `ingest`, and `line-of-inquiry propose` and `move`.

(If you need a verb or a flag tha…) → SHARED §1

Usage:
  feov-record edit [flags]

Flags:
      --accept           take red's prescribed fix EXACTLY as recorded on the gap named by --answers, instead of retyping it: the tool supplies --quote and --new from the mint, so you pass neither. Your --reason is still yours and still required — it is the argument for accepting. Refused when red prescribed no concrete text
      --answers gap-id   the gap id this edit responds to (G4) — the provenance join key; omit only for an edit that answers no gap
  -h, --help             help for edit
      --key string       → SHARED §6
      --new string       the text that span should become
      --quote string     the EXACT text from blue/report.md, quoted verbatim and NOTHING else — no section heading, no dash, no pipe: this whole string is matched against the report, so anything you prepend makes it match nothing. Name the section in --reason, where prose belongs. It is matched ACROSS the invisible anchor layer, and rejected if it contains a finding-marker or a citation anchor
      --reason string    → SHARED §2
      --reason-file -    → SHARED §3

